To implement these quality-of-life improvements, you can leverage native MUI features like autoSelect for your Autocompletes, and add an onKeyDown listener for the Debit/Credit shortcuts.
Here are the specific updates for each of your <Grid item> blocks. Replace your existing code for these fields with the snippets below:
### 1 & 2. Auto-Select First Suggestion on Tab
By combining autoHighlight (which highlights the first option) and adding autoSelect to your Autocomplete components, MUI will automatically pick the highlighted option when the user presses Tab.
**Branch Update:** Add autoSelect to the existing props.
```jsx
{/* Branch */}
<Grid item size={{ xl: 1.5, lg: 2 }}>
  <Autocomplete
    autoHighlight
    autoSelect // <-- ADDED: Selects the highlighted option on Tab/blur
    popupIcon={null}
    options={
      row.branch && !branchSearch.options.some((o) => o.code === row.branch.code)
        ? [row.branch, ...branchSearch.options]
        : branchSearch.options
    }
    // ... keep the rest of your Branch Autocomplete props exactly the same ...

```
